    {
      "id": "m21pp43",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7.1 Forest Cover"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Chhattisgarh possesses one of the highest forest cover percentages among Indian states, ranking 3rd in total forest area.",
        "The state is home to 3 National Parks: Indravati National Park, Kanger Valley National Park, and Guru Ghasidas (Sanjay) National Park.",
        "It hosts 11 Wildlife Sanctuaries, including Tamor Pingla (largest) and Badalkhol (smallest).",
        "Important endangered species in the region include the Wild Water Buffalo (State Animal) and the Bastar Hill Myna (State Bird).",
        "Major natural features like Chitrakote Waterfall (Niagara of India) and Tirathgarh Waterfall form core eco-tourism hubs."
      ],
      "id": "ml2m0i0"
    },
